  "description": "meme-id: adolf-hitler-meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image displays a black-and-white portrait of Adolf Hitler, a historical figure responsible for the Holocaust and genocide, with the text overlay 'every one is afraid of this man.' The intent is to evoke fear or intimidation by associating Hitler with universal fear, which is a direct and hateful attack on his legacy and the atrocities he committed. This meme is not merely ironic or satirical; it glorifies or romanticizes a mass murderer and war criminal, thereby promoting hate and dangerous historical revisionism. The juxtaposition of the image of Hitler with the text 'every one is afraid of this man' serves to normalize or even celebrate his terrifying reputation, which is inherently hateful and potentially harmful by encouraging the glorification of genocide and totalitarianism. This aligns with the 'Hateful' category as it directly attacks an individual based on his historical role as a perpetrator of mass violence and genocide.",
